   "id": "sanhedrin.13b.5",
   "daf": "13b",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "סְמִיכַת זְקֵנִים. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וְסָמְכוּ זִקְנֵי״ – יָכוֹל זִקְנֵי הַשּׁוּק? תַּלְמוּד לוֹמַר ״עֵדָה״.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: The «laying of hands by the Sages» is performed by a court of three judges according to Rabbi Shimon and five according to Rabbi Yehuda. «The Sages taught» in a baraita: The verse states: «“And the elders» of the congregation «shall lay» their hands on the head of the bull before the Lord” (Leviticus 4:15). One «might» have thought that the verse is referring to any «elders» in «the marketplace,» meaning people who are not members of the Sanhedrin. Therefore, «the verse states:» “Elders of the «congregation,”» meaning from among the leaders and judges of the people."
  }
 ],
